    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nOwners now get a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration-date year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) plus its getter/setter, following the existing `customerCode` pattern.\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 in `saveOwner`, assign `membershipNumber` (when unset) after `registrationDate` and `customerCode` are resolved, via a new `generateMembershipNumber` helper that builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` using `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` zero-padded to two digits.\n- **`resources/db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table in each dialect.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it into the REST response.\n\n## Tests\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes, asserting `membershipNumber == customerCode + \"-M\" + <YY>`.",
