    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into existing conventions:\n\n- `generateMembershipNumber(Owner)` sits right next to the analogous `generateCustomerCode(Owner)` private helper, uses the same `String.format` idiom, and carries a matching Javadoc \u2014 a maintainer would find it exactly where they'd expect.\n- The assignment in `saveOwner` follows the established guarded-assignment pattern (`if (... == null) owner.setX(generateX(owner))`) used for `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `namesakeCount`, and is correctly ordered after `customerCode` is generated since it depends on it.\n- Field + getter/setter on `Owner`, the column across all four schema dialects, and the `readOnly` OpenAPI property are all additive and consistent with how the neighboring `customerCode`/`householdId`/`namesakeCount` members are already modeled.\n\nNothing is duplicated and no class/method is becoming a catch-all; the logic lives in the appropriate service unit.",
